From 63cef437ec2cc294da4b265fc6f36232955d6400 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <tripleuworld@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:23:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi, arm64: dts: apple: j714s: take the GPU voltage
 bins from the ADT

The G17S voltage bins are fused per chip, so a J714s needed a device
tree naming its unit ("apple,j714s-gpu" for betizzel's, "-tripleu" for
TripleU613's) and an image only fit the unit it was built for.

The loader now copies the sgx node's perf-states, perf-states-sram,
perf-state-count, perf-state-table-count, afr-perf-states and
cs-perf-states to apple,adt-* properties of the gpu node (m1n1
patches/m1n1-installer 0005). "apple,j714s-gpu-adt" builds the board
from them: the generic M5 Pro profile (J716S) with this chip's core and
SRAM voltages for both main lanes and the auxiliary domain (SRAM
max(floor, core)). Frequencies, layout and voltages are checked against
that profile (same 14 frequencies, within 100 mV, at most 1150 mV) and
anything else refuses firmware init, as a missing property does.

t6050-j714s-gpu-adt{,-simpledrm}.dts boot on any J714s; the -tripleu
trees now include it with their own compatible.

Tested on TripleU613's J714s (macOS 27.3b1 stub, firmware 26C5035r):
the bins built from its ADT equal J714S_TRIPLEU exactly ("voltage bins
from the ADT (TripleU613's unit)"), and both firmware initdata were
acknowledged.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
